      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town hosts the historic Cidadela fortress, a 16th‑century citadel built during the Estado Novo to house authoritarian leaders.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cascais",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Roman fish‑salting tanks discovered along Rua Marquês Leal Pancada reveal Cascais’ ancient role in preserving marine food.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Cascais",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Guincho Beach to the northwest is famed for surfing, windsurfing, and kitesurfing thanks to strong Atlantic winds, while calmer eastern beaches suit sunbathers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
